Add `defaultTitle?: string` to DomRenderer, and in boot set `defaultTitle: document.title`. Or capture in applyMeta lazily on first call: `r.defaultTitle ??= document.title` before applying. Simpler; no index change. But at first apply after hydration, `document.title` is the SSR title (correct default). For a fresh resync after the title changed, defaultTitle would be the current (not original) title if not captured earlier. Set it at boot. We'll add `defaultTitle` to the interface and set in index.ts.

Implement helpers:
```ts
function windowFieldValue(strings, op) { return readString(strings, op.b); }
function applyMeta(op, strings, r) {
...
case CMD_SET_WINDOW_METADATA: {
  const value = readString(strings, op.b);
  switch (op.a) {
    case WINDOW_TITLE: document.title = value || (r.defaultTitle ?? "Pathland"); break;
    case WINDOW_DESCRIPTION: setMetaDescription(value); break;
    case WINDOW_LOCALE: if (value) document.documentElement.lang = value; else document.documentElement.removeAttribute("lang"); break;
  }
  break;
}
```
`setMetaDescription`:
```ts
let el = document.head.querySelector('meta[name="description"]');
if (!value) { el?.remove(); return; }
if (!el) { el = document.createElement("meta"); el.setAttribute("name","description"); document.head.appendChild(el); }
el.setAttribute("content", value);
```
Note `readString` may throw on bad offset; applyBatch catches. Fine.

Update applyBatch call `applyMeta(op, batch.strings, renderer)`.

