```
But for mount, we want initial values. `emitWindowMetadata(false)` after `lastWindowMetadata` empty → emits non-null; if value "" don't emit? If signal is null, skip. If signal non-null and value "" then emit clear (could be unnecessary). Fine.

In `mount`: after `tree = root.render(env)`, `this.windowMetadata = env.windowMetadata();`. Then `sink.beginFrame(); emitTheme(); emitWindowMetadata(false); emitNode(tree); sink.endFrame();` and after registerBindings call `registerWindowMetadataBindings()`.
In `renderFull`: after `emitTheme()` call `sink...`:
```java
emitWindowMetadata(true); // force: a reconnecting client may have missed a title change
```
But force should re-emit only fields with signals; if a field was cleared, lastWindowMetadata has ""; force re-emits "". Fine.

`registerWindowMetadataBindings`:
```java
for each field/signal:
  if (signal == null || isConstant(signal)) continue;
  EffectRef effect = Signals.effect(() -> {
