Now `PathlandSession` HTML injection. Current:
```java
return html
    .replace("<html>", "<html data-pathland-base=...>")
    .replace("</body>", ...);
```
Change to insert attributes before the first `>` of the `<html ...>` tag. Implement a helper:
```java
private static String injectHtmlAttrs(String html, String attrs) {
    int start = html.indexOf("<html");
    if (start < 0) return html;
    int end = html.indexOf('>', start);
    if (end < 0) return html;
    return html.substring(0, end) + attrs + html.substring(end);
}
```
Then:
```java
String attrs = " data-pathland-base=...";
return injectHtmlAttrs(html, attrs).replace("</body>", ...);
```
Careful: `<html` may match `<!DOCTYPE html>`? That's `<!DOCTYPE html>` — the substring `<html` is not present in `<!DOCTYPE html>` (there's a space before html, but no `<html`). Good.

