Add `use gtk::prelude::*;`? Check if already indirectly. We'll add explicitly after libadwaita prelude. Then sync function and calls.

In `run_with_pump_sized`, after window built, the title is moved into builder? `let window = ... .title(&title)`. `title` is the closure's captured String. We can clone it before: `let fallback_title = title.clone();` then use `fallback_title` in sync. Add after window creation.

Add helper:
```rust
fn sync_window_metadata(renderer: &Rc<RefCell<GtkRenderer>>, window: &gtk::ApplicationWindow, fallback_title: &str) {
    let meta = renderer.borrow().window_metadata().clone(); // WindowMeta clone (String)
    window.set_title(meta.title.as_deref().unwrap_or(fallback_title));
    if let Some(description) = meta.description.as_deref() {
        window.update_property(&[gtk::accessible::Property::Description(description)]);
    }
}
```
We can avoid clone of strings by borrowing but then call GTK while borrowed (fine, single-threaded). `let renderer = renderer.borrow(); let meta = renderer.window_metadata();` then use; but `window.set_title` is fine. However, holding the renderer borrow while calling GTK (which may trigger signals?) could re-enter. Safer clone values:
```rust
let (title, description) = {
  let r = renderer.borrow();
  let m = r.window_metadata();
  (m.title.clone(), m.description.clone())
};
```
Then apply.

Call after initial `pump_once` (before/after set_child) and in idle after `pump_once`. Add:
- initial: after `pump_once(&renderer, &pump);` then `sync_window_metadata(&renderer, &window, &fallback_title);`
- idle: inside `glib::idle_add_local(move || { ... pump_once(...); sync_window_metadata(&idle_renderer, &idle_window, &idle_title); ... })` — need clone window/title into idle closure. Add `let idle_window = window.clone(); let idle_title = fallback_title.clone();`.

Description accessible update: `window.update_property` requires `AccessibleExt`; with `gtk::prelude::*`. Also `Property::Description` expects `&str`. Good. If description is None, maybe clear by setting empty? We can skip. Full parity okay.

