parts.text:
For TS: in `PROP_LABEL` handling, if not media/icon, set `aria-label` if the element (or an input inside) is a control. Specifically:
- If `el` is `button` or the slider wrapper: set `el.setAttribute("aria-label", text)` for buttons; for slider wrapper, set the inner input's aria-label. We can generically:
```ts
if (el.matches("button, [role=button], input, select, textarea")) el.setAttribute("aria-label", text);
const input = el.querySelector("input,select,textarea");
if (input) input.setAttribute("aria-label", text);
```
But for TEXT_FIELD, `.pathland-label` span should still be updated; the LABEL is used as visible text. If we also set aria-label on the input, fine. The current logic prefers `.pathland-label` span and returns; add aria-label side-effect before.

Implement in `applyStringProperty`:
```ts
if (!media && !icon) {
  const control = el.matches("button,input,select,textarea,[role=button]") ? el : el.querySelector("button,input,select,textarea,[role=button]");
  if (control) control.setAttribute("aria-label", text);
}
```
Then continue with label span/text. For an empty label, remove aria-label.

Rust `aria_attrs`:
```rust
if let Some(label) = node.strings.get(&property_id::LABEL) {
    if !matches!(node.component, component_type::ICON | component_type::IMAGE | component_type::SLIDER) {
        attrs.push_str(&format!(" aria-label=\"{}\"", escape_html_attr(label)));
    }
}
```
Need `escape_html_attr` (defined later, usable). For empty label, skip (or emit empty? skip).
For SLIDER: in the SLIDER branch, compute label and put on input:
```rust
let aria = node.strings.get(&LABEL).map(|l| format!(" aria-label=\"{}\"", escape(l))).unwrap_or_default();
... <input ...{aria}>
```
But `aria` variable already used for the outer label; don't include slider in generic.

Also `aria_attrs` should not add aria-label to TEXT_FIELD? It's harmless. For TEXT (a `span`), `aria-label` overrides text; that's what accessibilityLabel means. Fine.

Then `aria-hidden="true"` on media wrapper.

